From 009abf5466ba87c169ead7b104ba41ba3d3c90f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aibox lab <aibox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:35:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fish_drama3: near real-time streaming for fixed voices

- stream_block: decode streamed audio in blocks (4 frames: 1.15x real
  time on gfx1151 Vulkan instead of 0.94x).
- Keep the system prefix (instruction and voice references) across
  chunks and requests: restore the linear-attention state saved after it
  and continue the prefill at its length (backbone and tower). Several
  voices' prefixes are kept on the host (prefix_slots, default 8).
- Encode each reference audio once per session.
- Dialogue: give each chunk the latest line of every speaker heard so
  far (speaker_context_frames), not only the previous chunk, so a
  speaker keeps its voice across turns.
- DRAMA3_TIMING / DRAMA3_CHECK_PREFIX print timings and compare the
  cached prefill with a full one.

First audio of a cloned voice: 1.24 s -> 0.28 s; same first token and
close first-frame distribution (KL <= 0.035) as a full prefill.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
